\f0\fs24 \cf0 ### The Golden Rule: Separating Code from Data\
\
To avoid confusion, remember one core rule:\
\
* **Code goes to Git** (tracked on GitHub, pulled onto the server).\
* **Data (SQLite) never goes to Git** (it lives only on the live server and in offline backups).\
\
---\
\
### Part 1: How to Keep Track of Local, Git, and Live\
\
Think of the workflow as a simple one-way pipeline: **Local Mac 
\f1 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  GitHub 
\f1 \uc0\u8594 
\f0  Oracle Live Server**.\
\
```\
[Local Mac] \uc0\u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 (git push)\u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 
\f1 \uc0\u9658 
\f0  [GitHub] \uc0\u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 (git pull)\u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 
\f1 \uc0\u9658 
\f0  [Oracle Server]\
     \uc0\u9474                                                                \u9474 \
 (Dev/Test)                                                    (Live Guests)\
\
```\
\
**1. Development (Local Mac):**\
\
* Work on code features, UI, or bugs locally.\
* Test with `php artisan serve` and `npm run dev`.\
* Commit and push changes:\
```bash\
git add .\
git commit -m "feat: added new feature"\
git push origin main\
\
```\
\
\
\
**2. Deployment (Oracle Server):**\
\
* SSH into your server:\
```bash\
ssh -i ~/.ssh/oracle_gh310.key ubuntu@134.185.83.115\
\
```\
\
\
* Pull the latest code and refresh:\
```bash\
cd /var/www/gh310-pms\
git pull origin main\
npm run build\
php artisan optimize:clear\
\
```\
\
\
* Your live database remains untouched while the code updates instantly.\
\
